# The app document must not be framed (bead qrcode-22b): frame-ancestors is header-only, so a
# <meta> CSP cannot carry it, and the result panel's "Return" (x-callback) and "Open" buttons are
# clickjackable once the document can be framed. Referrer-Policy (bead qrcode-igx) keeps the app
# URL - which can carry an x-callback-url destination or a kill-switch consent token - away from
# cross-origin receivers entirely; the document also pins it in a <meta> tag for hosts that do
# not read this file. This file is the static-host form of the policy (Netlify / Cloudflare Pages
# read `_headers`); any other host must send these three headers itself - see the "Framing" and
# "Referrer-Policy" sections in README.md.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: same-origin
